<title>FRANCE: Bull stock rises on smart card contract.</title>
<headline>Bull stock rises on smart card contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in computer group Bull were sharply higher on Tuesday on a report it won a contract along with two other firms to supply electronic smart cards for French citizens under the national health plan.</p>
<p>The newspaper La Tribune said Bull, Schlumberger and CP Oberthur will supply 15 million &quot;Vitale 1&quot; cards under the first stage of the project.</p>
<p>Shares in Bull, which had no immediate comment on the report, were 7.90 percent higher at 64.20 francs at 1118 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
